FILE: ChangeLog.md
FEATURE: cshapes-rectangle-fixes
DATE: 2026-10-11
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'marquee-module' (uncommitted at the time)

REASON
One Added bullet (config.radius) after the Marquee entries, and seven Fixed bullets at the end of
the v4.0.0-beta Fixed section, written from the consumer's side.

OLD_SECTION
- Marquee guide (doc/marquee.md) and runnable example (examples/marquee/)
...
- ModalDisplayer's split effect no longer shows browser-autofilled fields ...

## Removed

NEW_SECTION
- Marquee guide (doc/marquee.md) and runnable example (examples/marquee/)
- CShapes rectangles take `config.radius` for rounded corners, on both `fixedRectangle()` and `animatedRectangle()`; the line keeps one even thickness all the way round
...
- ModalDisplayer's split effect no longer shows browser-autofilled fields ...
- CShapes `animatedRectangle()` accepts a numeric `iterationCount`; ...
- CShapes rectangles are sharp on high-density screens; ...
- CShapes `animatedRectangle()` no longer re-strokes every earlier frame's rectangle ...
- Calling `draw()` again on a running `animatedRectangle()` restarts it; ...
- A repeating `animatedRectangle()` no longer jumps at the start of each cycle ...
- `animatedRectangle()` with an easing that does not end on exactly 1 now finishes ...
- `animatedRectangle().draw()` no longer requires the canvas to have an id

## Removed
